<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Andreyevich of Mozhaysk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Ivan of Mozhaysk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Andreyevich was prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozhaysk">Mozhaysk</a>, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow</a>. In the Muscovite civil war he joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-shemyaka">Dmitry Shemyaka</a>, and in 1446 he helped seize Grand Prince Vasily II at the Trinity Monastery, after which Vasily was blinded. When Vasily regained power, Mozhaysk was taken in 1454 and Ivan fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>.</p></div>
